# Selection anchors are byte offsets on Unicode scalar boundaries.
to get the UI text hit at {UI point:point} in {a pointer to UI view:view} limited to {a pointer to UI text source:scope}:
    set result to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run)
    set distance to 1.0e30
    set covering to the UI hit at point in view
    set run to view's texts
    loop while run != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
        set visible to true
        if covering != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout):
            set visible to run's paint serial >= covering's paint serial
        if scope != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
            set visible to visible and (run's source = scope)
        if run's source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
            set visible to visible and (the UI element (run's source's element) is enabled in (view's instance))
        if visible and ((run's generation = view's paint count) and (point is inside (run's clip))):
            set local to UI text position of point in run
            set width to the maximum of 8.0 and (the width of (run's text) using (run's typeface))
            set box to UI box at (run's origin's x) (run's origin's y - run's typeface's size) sized width (run's typeface's size + 5)
            set inside to local is inside box
            if run's source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
                set inside to (local's y >= box's y) and (local's y < (box's y + box's height))
            if inside:
                set candidate to 0.0
                if run's source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
                    set candidate to the maximum of 0.0 and (the maximum of (run's origin's x - local's x) and (local's x - (run's origin's x + (the width of (run's text) using (run's typeface)))))
                set take to true
                if result != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
                    if result's source = run's source:
                        set take to candidate <= distance
                if take:
                    set result to run
                    set distance to candidate
        set run to run's next
    return result

to get the UI text hit at {UI point:point} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    return the UI text hit at point in view limited to (@intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source))

to get the nearest UI text to {UI point:point} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set result to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run)
    set distance to 1.0e30
    set run to view's texts
    set source to view's selection's caret source
    loop while run != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
        set allowed to true
        if source != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
            if source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
                set allowed to run's source = source
            else:
                set allowed to run's source's element = @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)
        if run's source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
            set allowed to allowed and (the UI element (run's source's element) is enabled in (view's instance))
        if view's selection's limit != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
            set allowed to allowed and (run's source = view's selection's limit)
        if (run's generation = view's paint count) and allowed:
            set local to UI text position of point in run
            set top to run's origin's y - run's typeface's size
            set vertical to the maximum of 0.0 and (the maximum of (top - local's y) and (local's y - (top + run's typeface's size)))
            set horizontal to the maximum of 0.0 and (the maximum of (run's origin's x - local's x) and (local's x - (run's origin's x + (the width of (run's text) using (run's typeface)))))
            set candidate to vertical * 1000.0 + horizontal
            if candidate < distance:
                set distance to candidate
                set result to run
        set run to run's next
    return result

to select UI text at {UI point:point} in {a pointer to UI text run:run} extending {boolean:extend} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if view's selection's caret source != run's source:
        set view's input context's active to false
        set view's selection's composing to false
        set view's selection's composition to ""
    set local to UI text position of point in run
    set caret to run's start + (the UI text byte at (local's x - run's origin's x) in run)
    if run's source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
        if view's selection's anchor source != run's source:
            set extend to false
    else if view's selection's anchor source != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
        if view's selection's anchor source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
            set extend to false
    if extend = false:
        set view's selection's anchor source to run's source
        set view's selection's anchor to caret
    if (view's selection's caret source != run's source) or (view's selection's caret != caret):
        set view's damaged to true
    set view's selection's caret source to run's source
    set view's selection's caret to caret
    set view's selection's vertical to false
    set view's reveal caret to true

to handle UI text pointer at {UI point:point} over {a pointer to UI layout:hot} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if (view's down != view's was down) and view's down:
        set run to the UI text hit at point in view limited to (view's selection's limit)
        if hot != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout):
            if (the UI element (hot's node) is interactive in (view's instance)) and ((the UI element (hot's node) is a text control) = false):
                set inline to false
                if run != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
                    set inline to run's control = hot
                if inline = false:
                    set run to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run)
        if run = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
            clear UI selection in view
        else:
            set extend to ((view's modifiers bitwise and 1) != 0) and (view's selection's anchor source != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source))
            select UI text at point in run extending extend in view
            set view's selection's dragging to true
    else if view's selection's dragging and view's down:
        set run to the nearest UI text to point in view
        if run != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
            select UI text at point in run extending true in view
    if view's down = false:
        set view's selection's dragging to false

to commit UI text {string:updated} selecting {integer:anchor} through {integer:caret} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set composing to view's selection's composing
    set source to view's selection's caret source
    require condition (the UI element (source's element) accepts edits in (view's instance)) reporting "Only writable UI text can be committed"
    set entry to the UI value for (source's element) in (view's instance)
    set changed to record UI text edit in (the address of (entry's text state)) replacing with updated from (view's selection's anchor) through (view's selection's caret) selecting anchor through caret
    set view's selection's anchor to anchor
    set view's selection's caret to caret
    set source's text to entry's text
    set view's selection's vertical to false
    set view's selection's composition to ""
    set view's selection's composing to false
    set view's reveal caret to true
    set view's damaged to true
    if changed:
        activate (source's element) belonging to (source's element) in (view's instance)
    if composing and (view's instance's description's kind = 40):
        reflow the UI document in view

to replace UI text selection with {string:inserted} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set source to view's selection's caret source
    require condition (source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)) reporting "Only editable UI text can be replaced"
    set entry to the UI value for (source's element) in (view's instance)
    set start to the minimum of (view's selection's anchor) and (view's selection's caret)
    set end to the maximum of (view's selection's anchor) and (view's selection's caret)
    set filtered to UI text accepted from inserted by (source's element)
    set updated to ((the substring of (entry's text) from 0 spanning start bytes) + filtered) + (the substring of (entry's text) from end spanning (entry's text's length - end) bytes)
    commit UI text updated selecting (start + filtered's length) through (start + filtered's length) in view

to get the UI input source for {integer:epoch} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set candidate to view's selection's caret source
    set context to view's input context
    set empty to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source)
    if ((candidate = empty) or (view's keyboard focus = false)) or (view's active = false):
        return empty
    if (the UI element (candidate's element) is enabled in (view's instance)) = false:
        return empty
    if (context's active = false) or ((epoch != context's epoch) or (candidate's element != context's element)):
        return empty
    if (the UI element (candidate's element) accepts edits in (view's instance)) = false:
        return empty
    if (context's byte anchor != view's selection's anchor) or (context's byte caret != view's selection's caret):
        return empty
    if (the UI value for (candidate's element) in (view's instance))'s text != context's text:
        return empty
    return candidate

to receive platform UI text {string:updated} for {integer:epoch} selecting {integer:anchor} through {integer:caret} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set source to the UI input source for epoch in view
    if source = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
        return nothing
    set first to the UTF-8 byte offset of UTF-16 position anchor in updated
    set last to the UTF-8 byte offset of UTF-16 position caret in updated
    require condition ((first succeeded) and (last succeeded)) reporting "A platform text selection splits a Unicode character"
    set filtered to UI text accepted from updated by (source's element)
    set left to UI text accepted from (the substring of updated from 0 spanning (first's position) bytes) by (source's element)
    set right to UI text accepted from (the substring of updated from 0 spanning (last's position) bytes) by (source's element)
    commit UI text filtered selecting (left's length) through (right's length) in view

to receive UI composition {string:content} for {integer:epoch} at phase {integer:phase} selecting {integer:anchor} through {integer:caret} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set source to the UI input source for epoch in view
    if source = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
        return nothing
    if phase = 0:
        set view's selection's composing to false
        set view's selection's composition to ""
    else:
        if phase = 1:
            set view's selection's composing to true
            set view's selection's composition start to the minimum of (view's selection's anchor) and (view's selection's caret)
            set view's selection's composition end to the maximum of (view's selection's anchor) and (view's selection's caret)
        else:
            require condition ((phase = 2) and (view's selection's composing)) reporting "A composition update has no active composition"
        set first to the UTF-8 byte offset of UTF-16 position anchor in content
        set last to the UTF-8 byte offset of UTF-16 position caret in content
        require condition ((first succeeded) and (last succeeded)) reporting "A composition selection splits a Unicode character"
        set filtered to UI text accepted from content by (source's element)
        set left to UI text accepted from (the substring of content from 0 spanning (first's position) bytes) by (source's element)
        set right to UI text accepted from (the substring of content from 0 spanning (last's position) bytes) by (source's element)
        set view's selection's composition to filtered
        set view's selection's composition anchor to left's length
        set view's selection's composition caret to right's length
    set view's reveal caret to true
    set view's damaged to true
    if view's instance's description's kind = 40:
        reflow the UI document in view
    else:
        refresh UI text geometry for source in view

to restore UI text history in {a pointer to UI view:view} forward {boolean:forward}:
    set source to view's selection's caret source
    set entry to the UI value for (source's element) in (view's instance)
    set edit to entry's undo
    if forward:
        set edit to entry's redo
    if edit = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text edit):
        return nothing
    if forward:
        set entry's redo to edit's next
        set edit's next to entry's undo
        set entry's undo to edit
        set entry's text to edit's after
        set view's selection's anchor to edit's after anchor
        set view's selection's caret to edit's after caret
    else:
        set entry's undo to edit's next
        set edit's next to entry's redo
        set entry's redo to edit
        set entry's text to edit's before
        set view's selection's anchor to edit's anchor
        set view's selection's caret to edit's caret
    set source's text to entry's text
    set view's reveal caret to true
    activate (source's element) belonging to (source's element) in (view's instance)

to [navigate UI text in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set source to view's selection's caret source
    set key to view's key press
    set command to ((view's modifiers bitwise and 10) != 0) and ((view's modifiers bitwise and 4) = 0)
    set shift to (view's modifiers bitwise and 1) != 0
    if (((key = 262) or (key = 263)) or ((key = 268) or (key = 269))) or ((key = 264) or (key = 265)):
        set position to view's selection's caret
        set row to the UI caret row for source at position in view
        if key = 268:
            set position to row's start
            if command:
                set position to 0
        if key = 269:
            set position to row's end
            if command:
                set position to source's text's length
        if (shift = false) and (view's selection's anchor != view's selection's caret):
            if key = 263:
                set position to the minimum of (view's selection's anchor) and (view's selection's caret)
            if key = 262:
                set position to the maximum of (view's selection's anchor) and (view's selection's caret)
        else:
            if key = 263:
                set position to the previous UTF8 boundary before position in (source's text)
            if (key = 262) and (position < source's text's length):
                set position to (the UTF8 character at position in (source's text))'s next
        if (key = 264) or (key = 265):
            set direction to 1
            if key = 265:
                set direction to -1
            set position to the UI vertical destination from (view's selection's caret) in source toward direction in view
        else:
            set view's selection's vertical to false
        set view's selection's caret to position
        set view's reveal caret to true
        if shift = false:
            set view's selection's anchor to position
        set view's damaged to true
        consume the UI key in view
    if key = 257:
        consume the UI key in view
    if key = 32:
        if the UI element (source's element) accepts edits in (view's instance):
            set view's key press to -1
        else:
            consume the UI key in view
    if key = 256:
        clear UI selection in view
        consume the UI key in view
        set view's damaged to true

to handle UI [text] keys in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if view's active = false:
        set view's key press to -1
        return nothing
    set source to view's selection's caret source
    if source = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source):
        return nothing
    set control to source's element != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)
    set editable to false
    if control:
        if (the UI element (source's element) is enabled in (view's instance)) = false:
            set view's key press to -1
            set view's typed text to ""
            return nothing
        synchronize editable UI text source in view
        refresh UI text geometry for source in view
        set editable to the UI element (source's element) accepts edits in (view's instance)
    if view's selection's composing:
        set view's key press to -1
        return nothing
    set command to ((view's modifiers bitwise and 10) != 0) and ((view's modifiers bitwise and 4) = 0)
    set shift to (view's modifiers bitwise and 1) != 0
    if command:
        if editable and ((view's key press = 90) or (view's key press = 89)):
            restore UI text history in view forward ((view's key press = 89) or shift)
            consume the UI key in view
        if view's key press = 65:
            set first to source
            set last to source
            if (control = false) and (view's selection's limit = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source)):
                set first to view's texts' source
                set last to view's last text's source
            set view's selection's anchor source to first
            set view's selection's anchor to 0
            set view's selection's caret source to last
            set view's selection's caret to last's text's length
            consume the UI key in view
            set view's damaged to true
            set view's reveal caret to true
        if (view's key press = 67) or (view's key press = 88):
            set text to the selected UI text in view
            if text's length > 0:
                @intrinsic("call pointer", view's driver's copy, nothing, view, the data of text, text's length)
            if editable and (view's key press = 88):
                replace UI text selection with (the string form of "") in view
            consume the UI key in view
    if editable:
        if view's typed text's length > 0:
            replace UI text selection with (view's typed text) in view
            set view's typed text to ""
        set key to view's key press
        if the UI element (source's element) is multiline:
            if key = 257:
                replace UI text selection with (the string form of "\n") in view
            if key = 258:
                replace UI text selection with (the string form of "    ") in view
            if (key = 257) or (key = 258):
                consume the UI key in view
        if (key = 259) or (key = 261):
            if view's selection's anchor = view's selection's caret:
                if key = 259:
                    set view's selection's anchor to the previous UTF8 boundary before (view's selection's caret) in (source's text)
                else if view's selection's caret < source's text's length:
                    set view's selection's anchor to (the UTF8 character at (view's selection's caret) in (source's text))'s next
            replace UI text selection with (the string form of "") in view
            consume the UI key in view
    if control:
        if editable = false:
            set view's typed text to ""
        navigate UI text in view
